\paragraph{Horizontal coupling}
\label{sec:riccati-per-axis-limits}
Small tilt errors leak gravity into horizontal acceleration as
\begin{equation}
 \vct\varepsilon_{a,H}\simeq
 \begin{bmatrix}g\,\delta\theta_y\\-g\,\delta\theta_x\end{bmatrix}
 +\vct b_{a,H}+\vct n_H.
 \label{eq:riccati-axis-tilt-leak}
\end{equation}
There is no corresponding first-order vertical term. The scalar SpectralMSE
reduction omits this coupling and cannot alone determine horizontal tuning.
The factors in \eqref{eq:fus-rs-anisotropy} are applied in world NED;
their surge/sway interpretation is restricted to the zero-yaw records.

\subsection{Bias tracking}
For the medium JONSWAP sea, ten-seed OU--III accelerometer-bias RMS is
$0.0632\pm0.0330$~\si{m.s^{-2}} and gyroscope-bias RMS is
$(1.19\pm0.16)\times10^{-4}$~\si{rad.s^{-1}} over the final \SI{900}{s}.
Bias states also absorb model error; smooth estimates therefore do not
establish physical bias identifiability. The fixed-temperature, random-walk
truth deliberately differs from the slow Gauss--Markov estimator prior.
The ideal-sensor ablation in Sec.~\ref{sec:model-mismatch-ablation}
isolates the resulting deterministic residual.
