\subsection{Hard-iron correction}
\label{sec:mag-hi-results}
The matched on/off ablation uses one sensor-error draw on each of the eight
RAO records, scored over the final \SI{900}{s}
(Table~\ref{tab:mag-hi-yaw}). Arithmetic mean yaw RMS falls from
\SI{1.945}{\degree} to \SI{0.479}{\degree}; the worst-record RMS falls from
\SI{2.064}{\degree} to \SI{0.815}{\degree}. OU--II uses the same correction.
Misalignment-dominated draws can regress: unmodeled distortions may alias
into the additive fit while passing its residual gate. This is not a
complete magnetometer calibration.

\input{w3d-hard-iron-results-generated.tex-part}

\subsection{Embedded portability}
\label{sec:real-hardware-platform}
The estimator compiles and executes on the M5Stack AtomS3R (ESP32--S3)
with calibrated MEMS input (Fig.~\ref{fig:atoms3r-platform}). This establishes
source portability. Processor load, memory, power, deadline margin, thermal
performance, and externally referenced displacement accuracy were not measured.
\begin{figure}[!t]
  \centering
  \includesvg[width=0.25\columnwidth,inkscapelatex=false]{AtomS3R_device}
  \caption{M5Stack AtomS3R embedded validation target.}
  \label{fig:atoms3r-platform}
\end{figure}
